$$ Run the savestate harness under the debugger and name whatever kills it.
$$
$$ The harness crashes on its first cycle in about a second, so unlike the game
$$ there is no repro to perform - launch it, let it die, read the stack.
$$
$$ Deliberately no "sxe av". Mono implements null checks in hardware and handles
$$ the resulting access violations itself, so first-chance AVs are routine here
$$ and breaking on them stops the run on a non-event - which is exactly what the
$$ first version of this script did. Second chance means nobody handled it.

.symfix+ f:\rbo_fabre_proto\d3d9_sw\symbols-cache
.sympath+ f:\rbo_fabre_proto\d3d9_sw
.reload

$$ These two are never legitimate, so they are worth a first-chance break: the
$$ state that explains a corrupted list is gone by second chance.
sxe c0000409
sxe c0000374

g

.echo ===FAULT===
r
.echo ===FAULTING STACK===
kv
.echo ===ALL THREADS===
~*k
.echo ===MODULES===
lm m mono*
.echo ===ANALYZE===
!analyze -v
.logflush
q
